\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sing praise to God who reigns above,
\par The God of all creation,
\par The God of power, the God of love,
\par The God of our salvation;
\par With healing balm my soul He fills,
\par And every faithless murmur stills:
\par To God all praise and glory.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. What God's almighty power hath made,
\par His gracious mercy keepeth;
\par By morning glow or evening shade
\par His watchful eye ne'er sleepeth;
\par Within the kingdom of His might,
\par Lo! all is just and all is right:
\par To God all praise and glory.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The Lord is never far away,
\par But, through all grief distressing,
\par An ever-present help and stay,
\par Our peace, and joy, and blessing;
\par As with a mother's tender hand,
\par He leads His own, His chosen band:
\par To God all praise and glory.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thus, all my toilsome way along,
\par I sing aloud Thy praises,
\par That men may hear the grateful song
\par My voice unwearied raises;
\par Be joyful in the Lord, my heart,
\par Both soul and body bear your part:
\par To God all praise and glory.
\par                                       Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

